libfprint is an open source library to handle fingerprint reader devices.

This build is a variant of libfprint that adds a native, from-scratch
FpDeviceClass driver for the Goodix 27c6:533c fingerprint sensor (the
"53xc"/GTLS encrypted match-on-host family), reverse-engineered and
built at https://github.com/daemonhorn/goodix-533c-re. It includes the
full default driver set plus goodix533c, and links OpenCV for SIGFM
(SIFT-based) fingerprint matching, which that driver uses for
enroll/verify/identify.

On FreeBSD, hardware testing confirmed sensor open() and raw reference-
frame capture against a real 27c6:533c device. Enroll/verify/identify
(the SIGFM matching path) has not been exercised against real
fingerprints on FreeBSD and is unverified here.

Not yet merged upstream, tracked as:
https://github.com/goodix-fp-linux-dev/libfprint/pull/40
